Feature: Data Standardization for delivery_dt in f_order table

  Background:
    Given the table "purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_order"
    And the column "delivery_dt" datatype is Decimal(38,0)
    And the acceptable date format is "yyyymmdd"

  Scenario: Successful transformation of delivery_dt
    Given delivery_dt values are in correct format and datatype
    When the SQL logic is applied to convert to Decimal(38,0)
    Then delivery_dt should maintain yyyymmdd format 
    And no transformation errors should occur

  Scenario Outline: Invalid delivery_dt format or datatype
    Given delivery_dt value "<delivery_dt>"
    When the SQL logic checks format and datatype
    Then an error message "Invalid datatype or format for delivery_dt" should be displayed
    And the record should not be processed for transformation

  Examples:
    | delivery_dt  |
    | 2024-09-10   |
    | 10/09/2024   |
    | timestamp    |

  Scenario Outline: Invalid date range in delivery_dt
    Given delivery_dt value "<delivery_dt>"
    When the SQL logic checks the date range
    Then an error message "Date not within acceptable range for delivery_dt" should be displayed

  Examples:
    | delivery_dt  |
    | 00000000     |
    | 99999999     |

  Scenario: Successful conversion and integration verification
    Given all delivery_dt values successfully converted to Decimal(38,0)
    And are in yyyymmdd format
    When integrated with external datasets
    Then the standardized data should align with reporting standards
    And integration should occur without errors

  Scenario Outline: Unhandled exceptions during transformation
    Given delivery_dt value "<delivery_dt>"
    When unexpected datatype or conversion error occurs
    Then an error message "Unhandled exception during delivery_dt transformation" should be logged

  Examples:
    | delivery_dt |
    | NULL        |
    | NaN         |
    | " "         |

  Scenario: Additional data cleansing requirements verification
    Given converted delivery_dt values
    When cleansing steps are applied if required
    Then delivery_dt should remain compliant with target table requirements
    And no additional cleansing errors should occur

  Scenario: Verification of SQL logic integration with other datasets
    Given integration requirement with "purgo_playground.purgo_playground.supply_chain_delivery"
    When the SQL logic executes
    Then the interaction with other datasets should be validated
    And no mismatched data should occur during the process
